  "methodology": "One Chrome, one Vite dev server; both builds load as ES modules into one page per repetition. Each configuration mounts its own visible 160x50 terminal (fit off, 10,000 lines scrollback, 1500x1000 host, stacked without overlap). Every round runs each configuration once in rotated order: (1) bulk: 32 MiB of SGR-colored log lines in 64 KiB chunks, each write awaited (parsed), then flush() (forced render + GPU fence), MiB/s; (2) GPU-fenced benchmark() dense and scroll, 512 frames each. Paired ratios divide each configuration by the reference measured in the same round. After the rounds, (3) stream: 2 s of 40 lines every 16 ms per configuration, counting render submissions (onRender), which are submissions, not display presentation. Screen reader on uses announcements \"always\", so worker sampling, diffing, mirror DOM and live-region updates all run.",
